<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 14.11 pct,M2 up 5.99 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 14.11 pct,M2 up 5.99 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 1.121 trillion levs on July 11 from 982.7 billion levs a week earlier and M2 increased to 4.271 trillion levs from 4.03 trillion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 5.22 percent to 4.492 trillion levs in the week to July 11.</p>
<p>Conversion of foreign currency-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixing of 1,000 levs per mark for July 4 and July 11, and 990.6 for June 27.</p>
<p>The lev was pegged at 1,000 per mark under an IMF-prescribed fixed exchange rate mechanism, known as currency board system, launched on July 1.</p>
<p>The system requires levs in circulation to be fully matched by the central bank's foreign exchange reserves.</p>
